docs/INFO_ITEM_DETAIL.md :: retarget :: **It re-reads itself while a command is open** (archiver#212): *closure* arrives on `content.artifacts` a bus round trip (~800ms) after issuance, so the POST's swap is always too early. `GET …/rep-spec-assignments` returns the same partial; the wrapper carries `hx-get` + `hx-trigger="every 2s"` + `hx-swap="outerHTML"` **only while some latest command is `requested`**, rendered from the same `latest_commands` the badges are, so the swap that lands a terminal state stops the polling. Bounded at two minutes (`POLL_WINDOW`; the reaper's six hours is too long for a forgotten tab), then a `role="status"` line says one is still open. A poll renders `swapped=False`: no focus move. **The poll always yields to an action** (archiver#220): `hx-sync="this:abort"` + `hx-disinherit="hx-sync"` on the wrapper, `hx-sync="closest #ii-rep-spec-assignments:drop"` on each action - UI.md § *A section that polls and takes actions*.
docs/INFO_ITEM_DETAIL.md :: retarget :: **Every outcome is a 200, and every outcome flashes** via `HX-Trigger: showFlash` - issued at `success` naming the rendered destination, a recorded `skipped` row at `warning` naming its reason (it also renders as state in the Replication column), and a refusal the service will not record - `not_active`, `no_active_source`, `no_revision`, `assignment_unreachable` - at `error`. Refusals are 200s rather than 422s because htmx discards a 4xx body (see UI.md § **Inline validation errors** and the STYLE.md rule it points at). The outcome→flash translation is `src/dashboard/replication_actions.py`, shared with the RepSpec-scoped twin (PAGES.md § **Replication Specifications**).
